        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1728-a1">

                <pb facs="1106" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg990"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the Minister for Foreign Affairs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor again to refer to
                    my notes Nos. 40 and 46 of the dates respectively of April 9 and April 18 last,
                    and to your excellency’s note No. S-3476, of the last-named date, to which said
                    note No. 46 was a reply, having reference to the matter of the Cocoa Grove
                    affair of July 4, 1912; and further to inform your excellency that I am now in
                    receipt of another cablegram from my Government vigorously insisting upon a
                    satisfactory and prompt settlement of this whole affair.</p>
                <p>With due regard to every consideration of courtesy and good will, I would assure
                    your excellency that the insistency and emphasis have been sincere with which I
                    have attempted to impress your excellency ever since coming to this mission with
                    the importance which my Government puts upon a full, satisfactory, and prompt
                    settlement by your excellency’s Government of our expectancies and demands in
                    this wretched affair; and I must respectfully ask that the patience of my
                    Government shall not be further unduly provoked in this matter.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.],</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Jennings Price</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
